WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.507
[Sylvia Earle]
<i>I see things that others do not,</i>

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.575
<i>a different world...</i>

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:13.680
<i>a world that's changed enormously
just in my lifetime.</i>

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.283
<i>My backyard was the Gulf of Mexico.</i>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.252
<i>That's where I first fell in love
with the ocean.</i>

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:23.456
<i>I think if others had the opportunity to
witness what I have seen in my lifetime</i>

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.058
<i>from thousands of hours underwater...</i>

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.728
<i>I would not seem like a radical at all.</i>

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:35.168
It's a pleasure to introduce a scientist,
an engineer, a teacher and an explorer.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.603
[applause]

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.072
<i>The ocean is dying.</i>

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:47.714
<i>All of us... we are the beneficiaries
of having burned through fossil fuels.</i>

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.149
<i>But at what cost?</i>

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:54.354 line:5%
<i>Sixty years ago,
when I began exploring the ocean,</i>

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.589
<i>no one imagined
that we could do anything to harm it.</i>

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:04.197
I saw the after influence of what
we can do to the natural world.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.567
<i>Think of the world without an ocean.</i>

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.769
You've got a planet a lot like Mars.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.305
<i>No ocean, no life.</i>

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.240
<i>No ocean, no us.</i>

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.712
[Hugh Downs] <i> In 1990, she became
the chief scientist for NOAA,</i>

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.182
<i>National Oceanic
and Atmospheric Administration.</i>

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.417
[Earle] <i> I went to one meeting...</i>

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.620
and I was never allowed to go again.
[laughs]

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.693
I feel that I must resign,
and as a private citizen,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>do what I can do with more freedom.</i>

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:42.302
She's not afraid to say, "You know what
you're doing, and it's wrong."

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.207
[Earle] <i> I really speak for the ocean.</i>

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:51.478
If we continue business as usual,
we're in real trouble.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.548
[James Cameron]
<i>She's made it her life's purpose</i>

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.218
to make sure everybody else
understands what's going on.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.056
[Fisher Stevens]
<i>Sylvia has a wish for the planet...</i>

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.624
<i>what she calls her Mission Blue.</i>

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:08.661
<i>Protect the ocean in the same way
we now protect the land.</i>

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:12.232
[Earle] <i> I wish for a global network
of marine protected areas</i>

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.434
<i>to save and restore the ocean.</i>

